      "sequence_position": 10,
      "problem": "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nGiven the matrix $A$ above, evaluate the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}^{T}\\,Ax$ when $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ into the expression for $Q(x),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}^{T}\\,Ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}14 & 13\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =55.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
